Step 3 is implemented in [learned_router.py](D:\_my_stuff\HACKATHON-08-2026\task2-Viktor\EHL-Hackathon-August-2026-Viktor\viktor-tumai-starter\scripts\learned_router.py:1).

It trains a depth-3 regression tree on the Step 1 structural outcome score using only first-call deployment features:

- first user-text length;
- first request’s estimated input size;
- tool count;
- image presence;
- explicit one-hot candidate-model indicators.

For each trajectory, it predicts the outcome under each sufficiently represented model, then selects the lowest-priced candidate whose prediction is at least `0.65` and within `0.05` of the logged-model prediction. The selected route keeps one model for the entire trajectory, preserving cache behavior.

It writes the standard `results/routes.jsonl` by default (optional second argument permits a different route-file name) and saves readable learned rules to `results/learned_tree_rules.txt`.

